      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "I found One Stop Utilities through an ad on ozbargain. They quoted me a 6.3kW system with Risen panels and a 5kW Goodwe inverter. Very prompt correspondence and I got the install done around a week after the solar homes approval from government. I believe the installers were subcontracted. Two guys turned up and they did a very neat job of installing the panels. I am an engineer and I got out the vic guidelines, and as far as I can tell it is all compliant. The inverter was installed next to my meterbox. This could have been a bit nicer as they did not run the conduit behind the brick veneer, however overall it is fairly neat/straight and is compliant.I turned the system on last week on an overcast Winter's day and produced way more power than I expected. My first good day in Winter is today and I have produced 14kWh between the sun coming up at 7.30 and 1pm right now.Overall I am very happy.",
